      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MIDNIGHT REVOLT (8) looks the one to beat after winning on debut at Scone over 1100m, holding on by a neck despite being unwanted in the market. She now steps up in grade, but the stable and jockey profile is strong and the single piece of race evidence has immediate upside. Maps well and will take holding out. SAUVITUDE (5) is the main danger after scoring at this track and trip first-up as favourite, with his Sale debut given extra merit after racing wide without cover on heavy ground. Can stalk the speed and go close. WON'THEARMECOMING (6) has been placed in all four starts and brings solid Class 1 and Class 2 Scone form, although this is harder company after being a beaten favourite last time. DONWON (1) will relish the sharp drop in class after savaging the line for a sound fourth over 1100m at Canterbury in BM78 grade. Claim helps and sure to be thereabouts.",
